  "_items_source": {
    "document": "AQA A-level Computer Science (7517) specification: subject content sections 4.1-4.13 (A-level only content; the NEA, 4.14, is declared out of scope)",
    "url": "https://filestore.aqa.org.uk/resources/computing/specifications/AQA-7516-7517-SP-2015.PDF",
    "version": "Version 1.6 (31 July 2023), the current version linked from aqa.org.uk/7517, itemised 2026-09-27",
    "itemised_on": "2026-09-27",
    "numbering": "AQA's own numbered content references, at a teaching-sized grain. AQA's specification numbers this content to four levels in places (e.g. 4.1.1.1-4.1.1.16, 4.2.2.1.1-4.2.2.1.4, 4.9.4.1-4.9.4.11); where several of AQA's own adjacent sub-bullets form one natural lesson (e.g. 4.1.1.10-4.1.1.12 on subroutines/parameters/return values, or 4.5.6.1-4.5.6.3 on analogue/digital conversion), this course codes that lesson under the first sub-bullet's reference and teaches the rest of the range alongside it; the item's own title names everything it covers. 4.2's third-party-queue/stack operation lists (4.2.2.1.1-4.2.2.1.4, 4.2.3.1.1-4.2.3.1.5) are similarly taught as one item each (4.2.2.1 Queues, 4.2.3.1 Stacks). 4.10 (Databases) and 4.11 (Big Data) are numbered by AQA as unnumbered content/additional-information tables rather than sub-bulleted lists; this course assigns them working reference numbers 4.10.1-4.10.5 and 4.11.1 in the specification's own topic order. Section 4.14 (the NEA) is out of scope; see the notice below."
  },
